{
  "openapi": "3.1.0",
  "info": {
    "title": "Hito API",
    "version": "1.0.0",
    "summary": "Contract-to-cash for freelancers, on PayPal.",
    "description": "Hito reads a freelance contract, invoices each milestone through PayPal, estimates the probability that an invoice is never paid, asks for the money in the register that probability deserves, and splits what arrives among collaborators.\n\nTwo guardrails are part of the API contract rather than the UI:\n\n* `POST /api/milestones/{milestone_id}/deliver` runs an independent reviewer before PayPal is called. It can return `stage: \"blocked\"` (nothing is created) or `stage: \"hold\"` (a human must pass `override: true`).\n* `POST /api/payouts/{payout_id}/approve` only sends items above `PAYOUT_APPROVAL_THRESHOLD_USD` when their ids appear in `approved_item_ids`.\n\nWith no credentials configured the API is fully functional against an in-process PayPal gateway and a deterministic agent engine; `GET /api/status` always says which mode is live.",
    "license": {
      "name": "MIT",
      "url": "https://opensource.org/licenses/MIT"
    }
  },
